rie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="319461" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/61/319461/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I64ef50e3400cb5165f22aa12e6c412d869ccf22a" commit="203bac9054ed352c31e20faac75cda4e25e1a8cc" commit_message="faft: Change the spi_voltage config of Celes to pp3300  It makes flashrom able to detect the SPI flash on servo v3.  BUG=None TEST=Manually call host.firmware_install() which sets the spi_voltage value.  Change-Id: I64ef50e3400cb5165f22aa12e6c412d869ccf22a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323824 Commit-Ready: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: danny chan &lt;dchan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323824" owner_email="waihong@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/24/323824/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia498b44aaf9c65ab6c072c4c7b47b22c87baba9e" commit="6154038a193ce501455aabfa9248c87e2b16b5cc" commit_message="brillo: Create an audio test suite.  Create an audio test suite for audio specific brillo tests and add tests to it.  BUG=26739178 TEST=test_droid.py suite:brillo-audio passes  Change-Id: Ia498b44aaf9c65ab6c072c4c7b47b22c87baba9e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323418 Commit-Ready: Ralph Nathan &lt;ralphnathan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ralph Nathan &lt;ralphnathan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Gilad Arnold &lt;garnold@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323418" owner_email="ralphnathan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/18/323418/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I54e61f417ad506eb3b4cd5d0652f64eed9a28a17" commit="8e5f38e2377f269a64532892866a6a1abe25f7b5" commit_message="chip: it83xx: fix EC interrupt vector registers issue  We have a limitation for EC interrupt vector registers. System may read incorrect interrupt number in ISR so we need to add a workaround to prevent it.  The following is a example that got incorrect interrupt number: 1. REG IVCTx = 0x10. (no interrupt pending) 2. EC INT6 interrupt occurs (IVCTx = 0x16) and jump to ISR. 3. Read interrupt vector register to determine interrupt number. 4. Higher priority interrupt of same interrupt group occurs    (for example: INT134, IVCTx = 0x96) while the system is reading the    interrupt vector register for EC INT6, we may end up with an incorrect    interrupt number between 0x16 and 0x96.  Signed-off-by: Dino Li &lt;dino.li@ite.com.tw&gt;  BRANCH=none BUG=none TEST=1. EC interrupts work normally: WUI (GPIO interrupt), timer, uart,         LPC, I2C, and PECI.      2. Console command 'taskinfo'.  Change-Id: I54e61f417ad506eb3b4cd5d0652f64eed9a28a17 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/322097 Commit-Ready: Dino Li &lt;dino.li@ite.com.tw&gt; Tested-by: Dino Li &lt;dino.li@ite.com.tw&gt; Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="322097" owner_email="dino.li@ite.com.tw" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/97/322097/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4d66a8901f922df34d35064175e34133483a7196" commit="50bbe835577a45207997cdbe1ff057c41254c5a6" commit_message="l